This file is deliberately not a plist any more.

It used to be a static property list with an absolute path baked into it,
pointing at a Desktop folder. That path stopped being true the moment the repo
moved, and macOS refused to run it anyway, because launchd agents cannot read
Desktop, Documents or Downloads:

    /bin/bash: .../run_scan.sh: Operation not permitted

install.sh now generates the plist at install time from wherever the repo
actually is, and refuses to install at all if the repo sits in a
macOS-protected directory rather than failing silently every Monday morning.
